*8: Detailed comments for the authors
  This paper presents SPG-Net, a novel deep learning model for myocardial i=
nfarction (MI) localization from ECG data. The authors introduce several in=
novative techniques, including class-specific adaptive classifiers and a gr=
aph-spatiotemporal attention mechanism, which show promising results in han=
dling class imbalance. The paper is well-structured, the motivations and in=
novations are clearly presented. The minor issues are listed as follows:
1.	Page 1, Section II, Part A, in the second line of the first paragraph, "=
(MI)" is redundant and should be deleted.
2.	The Pearson correlation threshold (=CE=B8) used in graph construction is=
 not clearly explained. Please clarify how it was determined.
3.	In Section III, Part A, the description of the Dynamic Bias Weight (DBW)=
 mechanism, more detailed information on how to select parameter =CE=BBi sh=
ould be appropriately supplemented.

