*8: Detailed comments for the authors
  This paper introduces SPG-Net, a structure-aware spatiotemporal graph net=
work that significantly advances the state-of-the-art in MI localization fr=
om ECG signals. The method combines anatomical priors and spatiotemporal de=
pendencies effectively, outperforming other models in several key areas. Th=
e paper is well written, the motivations and objectives are clearly present=
ed, however, there are some minor concerns that should be addressed.
1.	"MCA-net", "MLresnet" and =E2=80=9CMRM-net=E2=80=9D appear in Tables II =
and III, which do not seem to be completely inconsistent with the names of =
the baseline models "MCA-Net", "ML-ResNet" and =E2=80=9CMRM-Net=E2=80=9D de=
scribed in Section IV-B.
2.	The last paragraph in Section III-A, a completely duplicated sentence ap=
peared:=20
 =E2=80=9CThe full set {G_{\text{prior}}^{(k)} forms the structural prior u=
sed by the GSCA module.=E2=80=9D
3.	Some figures are too small to see clearly (e.g. Fig. 3 and Fig. 4). It i=
s recommended to enlarge the images appropriately and use larger fonts.


